    "body": "Introduce the `xr + n < p` condition in the step where it is needed, namely right before switching from integer equality to equality modulo p, and explain why it is required there. Write congruences as `a == b (mod m)`, because `a mod p == b` reads as if `mod p` were an operator applied to the left-hand side only.\r\n\r\nAlso reword the comment at the `p - n` check: the check is needed for correctness, not merely an optimization.\r\n\r\nMade these improvements when trying to understand the background of #1948.",
